**Purpose-built silicon is not better in these cases:**

- decode cost at ordinary interactive speed (about equal)
- prefill ({{ x(I.prefill.s_over_g0_per_usd, 2) }} the GPUs per dollar)
- demand below about {{ n(I.demand.breakeven_tokens_per_day.s / 1e12, 1) }} trillion tokens a day
- small sparse models
- the longest contexts on cheap KV memory
- a single request ({{ x(I.power_management.managed.over_g0_best_batch, 2) }} of the tokens per joule of a busy GPU cluster)

## Method

1. **Workload from the checkpoint.** We compute parameter counts, precisions and bytes per token
   from the safetensors headers. The results reproduce the published {{ bn(W.params.hub_total, 2) }} exactly
   ([01](docs/01_workload.md)).
2. **A GPU baseline calibrated to public data.** We fitted four constants to {{ CG.n_points }} published
   figures from two serving engines. The RMS error is {{ pct(CG.rms_log_error, 1) }}. The leave-one-out error has a median of
   {{ pct(CG.loo_median_abs_error, 1) }} and a worst value of {{ pct(CG.loo_max_abs_error) }} ([06](docs/06_simulator.md)). The GPU gets its best
   published setup, and we count its prefill load. We also model a software-only counterfactual on the same GPUs.
3. **A check on four real machines.** The machines are Llama 3.1 8B on a GPU, two SRAM machines and a fixed-weight
   chip. With public specifications as input, {{ CL.n_within }} of {{ CL.n }} predictions have an error of 30% or less. We report that as a
   failure. We use the published speeds, not our own assumption, to set the time per operation of the chip.
4. **Five platforms on one simulator.** The constants are the same where the physics is the same
   ([02](docs/02_design_rationale.md), [03](docs/03_architecture.md)).
5. **One block in silicon.** We wrote the NVFP4 block-scaled dot product in SystemVerilog. We checked it bit for bit
   against a reference on real expert weights. We synthesized it on an open 7 nm kit
   ([07](docs/07_silicon.md)).
6. **Predictions first.** We froze {{ PRE.predictions | length }} numeric predictions before simulation.
   {{ PR.inside }} of {{ PR.scored }} scored predictions are inside their range, and we list the misses
   ([00](docs/00_hypotheses.md)).
7. **Uncertainty.** {{ U.params | length }} inputs have ranges that we state. We moved them one at a time and all
   together ({{ MC.n }} draws). A napkin calculation is beside each headline ([napkin](docs/napkin.md)).
8. **Adversarial review.** Two fresh agents attacked a clean copy of the repo. [05](docs/05_limitations.md) gives their findings, our
   changes and the size of the headline change.

